1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,140
I don't want to be in high school anymore.

2
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:08,180
Can I go back to middle school, please?

3
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:10,560
How many times are you going to say that, dude?

4
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:13,220
I yearn for my motherland.

5
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:14,540
You can just say your hometown.

6
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:16,980
But you've got lots of pals at your new school.

7
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:19,980
Don't get me wrong, I'm not complaining about my friends.

8
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:22,680
It's more like I don't vibe with the school itself.

9
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:23,460
This news fest?

10
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:26,440
Yeah, it's always got this creepy, empty silence.

11
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,580
We could really use more dumbasses.

12
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:30,500
Not sure if I dig the implication there.

13
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:33,080
I don't mean idiots, I mean dumbasses.

14
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:36,460
Remember third year when we'd all have fun and be dumb after class?

15
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:38,260
Me, Yamada, and Niyu.

16
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,380
That's an all-star study group right there.

17
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:42,180
The good old stupid days.

18
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,360
Study group is kind of a stretch.

19
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:47,980
If anything, goofing off all the time was killing our brain cells.

20
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:49,460
Yeah, murder them all!

21
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:51,320
He's starting to freak me out.

22
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:52,940
None of us were in any club,

23
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:56,260
so we could just devote all of our would-be practice time to goof-maxing.

24
00:00:56,260 --> 00:00:57,680
We lifted up back then.

25
00:00:57,680 --> 00:00:59,620
We were cringe, but we were free!

26
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:02,020
And thinking back now, it's...

27
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:03,160
It's heavy, man.

28
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:04,620
Straight up monologuing, okay?

29
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:08,440
And Yamada thought he was too good for our paradise after he got a girlfriend.

30
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:09,640
Whack as hell.

31
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,820
Hey, don't turn me into the bad guy here!

32
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:18,580
Sometimes when the sun sets, I'll walk down the roads I took to middle school just to feel something.

33
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:19,740
You good, dude?

34
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:24,880
I hear our old choir songs echoing, and the tears just won't stop.

35
00:01:25,020 --> 00:01:26,300
Oh no, he's not good at all.

36
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:29,520
You have to treasure those precious moments while you've still got them,

37
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:32,380
because one day they'll slip through your fingers like sand.

38
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:34,220
So that's what Rihi said.

39
00:01:34,740 --> 00:01:36,200
My man is going through it.

40
00:01:36,420 --> 00:01:36,800
Sad.

41
00:01:37,460 --> 00:01:38,000
Huh?

42
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:40,320
He's just hung up on the past.

43
00:01:40,380 --> 00:01:41,120
It's not that deep.

44
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:42,440
Meany, bobeany.

45
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:44,860
Oh, my middle school was too fun.

46
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:46,020
My lobster was too buttery.

47
00:01:46,020 --> 00:01:47,240
My steak was too juicy.

48
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:50,800
By the way, whose bride idea was it to go and invite Suzuki?

49
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:52,380
Are you cool with that?

50
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:55,760
Yeah, I don't decide who she gets to hang out with.

51
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:58,640
Even thinking about it too much would be disrespectful,

52
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:00,500
because then it's like I don't trust her.

53
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:03,060
But thanks for worrying about us.

54
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:04,920
What is this?

55
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,040
What did you get so confident?

56
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:07,440
Is that bad?

57
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:09,700
Ugh, I hate you, bro.

58
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:10,400
What?

59
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:10,580
What?

60
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:40,560
I hate you, bro.

61
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:43,820
Sin, cosine, tangent

62
00:02:43,820 --> 00:02:46,980
心の角度が広がって

63
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:49,760
電流が走る一目惚れ

64
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:52,020
覚えていてフレーニング

65
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:55,740
純度100%の想いも

66
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:58,560
一心伝心させたいな

67
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:01,340
君とあたしは正反対

68
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:03,720
恋はいつも想定外

69
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:05,700
ねえねえ聞いて

70
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:09,700
言葉を尽くして君に伝えたいの

71
00:03:09,700 --> 00:03:12,700
心が体に追いついて

72
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:14,640
気づけば目で追ってる

73
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:17,940
眼鏡を外してさ

74
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:20,980
ちゃんと目を合わせてよ

75
00:03:20,980 --> 00:03:23,780
恋は走り出したの

76
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:26,760
放課後まで待てない

77
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:29,760
大事な言葉ほど

78
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:32,860
酸素を嫌うみたい

79
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:35,940
辞書にないあたしなりの言葉で

80
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:37,940
早く早く早く早く

81
00:03:37,940 --> 00:03:39,740
君に伝えなきゃね

82
00:03:39,740 --> 00:03:42,500
どういうふうに伝えなきゃ

83
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:43,740
言っていなきゃ

84
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:44,820
猛が見つけた

85
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:46,640
そうやって

86
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:46,840
や魔のにとことを

87
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:47,100
早くは

88
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:47,900
まだ我々は

89
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:49,320
やまま

90
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:50,440
たぶんは

91
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:52,840
元々が

92
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:53,640
想念ながら

93
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:54,700
引っかりする

94
00:03:54,700 --> 00:03:55,840
急ぎ

95
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:56,620
経擇

96
00:03:56,620 --> 00:03:57,320
これで

97
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,540
遇われて

98
00:03:58,540 --> 00:04:01,240
I won't ask any questions until he brings it up himself.

99
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:04,840
If it didn't go well, I would have no idea what to say.

100
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:07,940
And even if it did go well, I'd still have no idea what to say.

101
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:12,440
I'm such a jerk.

102
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:18,540
And now for a brief snowcap of Yamada's Festivod fun time.

103
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:21,440
Did you take this one?

104
00:04:21,840 --> 00:04:22,540
Uh-huh.

105
00:04:22,740 --> 00:04:24,240
Really? Sick.

106
00:04:28,540 --> 00:04:31,600
Come on, just spit it out, Nishi.

107
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:33,440
I'm sorry I'm a terrible texter.

108
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:36,080
I'm sorry I'm so weird that I made it seem like I hate you.

109
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:38,820
I'm so awkward I can't even apologize for being awkward.

110
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,400
Hey, listen, I...

111
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:45,240
Go ahead.

112
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:46,520
I'm sorry.

113
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:49,920
For texting you and all that.

114
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:54,360
If someone I didn't know asked me for my number, I'd be creeped out.

115
00:04:54,980 --> 00:04:57,380
I get it. I was coming on way too strong.

116
00:04:57,380 --> 00:05:00,080
I mean, who wants a stranger bothering them like that?

117
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:03,000
Point is, I gotta think harder before I act.

118
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:03,980
My bad.

119
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:07,080
Sorry, were you gonna say something?

120
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:08,020
Uh...

121
00:05:08,020 --> 00:05:09,860
I, uh...

122
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:11,380
I'm sorry too.

123
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:14,020
I'm not used to texting people.

124
00:05:14,460 --> 00:05:17,660
Up until now, I mostly just used my phone to talk to my parents.

125
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:21,180
I'll message home or someone every once in a while, but that's it.

126
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:29,260
I worry I'll write something weird, and I worry about typos or spend hours writing a stupid long text, and I worry about how long it is and how long it took to reply.

127
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:33,100
I would just talk on the phone, but I'm even worse at that than texting.

128
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:38,420
Still, despite all that stuff, I like texting you.

129
00:05:38,420 --> 00:05:45,660
I know I overthink everything because I'm scared of making mistakes, but I'm gonna try my best to find a way to stop doing that.

130
00:05:45,660 --> 00:05:49,500
We're total opposites.

131
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:53,900
Whenever you'd send something, I'd just text back right away without thinking.

132
00:05:54,420 --> 00:05:55,960
I never thought you said anything weird.

133
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:56,880
Not even once.

134
00:05:57,400 --> 00:06:02,080
Plus, I don't pick up on little details, so I probably wouldn't even notice if you goofed something up.

135
00:06:02,940 --> 00:06:04,960
Oh, you should practice on me.

136
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:06,200
I'll be your dummy.

137
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:08,040
I'm chill.

138
00:06:08,220 --> 00:06:09,980
You don't have to be scared of messing up with me.

139
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:11,320
I'm too dumb to notice.

140
00:06:11,660 --> 00:06:13,880
And if I ever get annoying, you could just tell me, okay?

141
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,780
Say, shut your yap trap, idiot.

142
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:16,420
Easy.

143
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:19,000
I never say that.

144
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:20,060
Not that way.

145
00:06:22,020 --> 00:06:23,300
Willst thou shish it?

146
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:24,940
What is that?

147
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:26,060
Am I a princess now?

148
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:29,720
Oh, Rihi, I forgot.

149
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:31,220
I gotta head out.

150
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:32,680
See her out, okay?

151
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:38,040
Is it cool if we talk at school, too?

152
00:06:39,380 --> 00:06:40,380
Yes, of course!

153
00:06:41,260 --> 00:06:41,740
Nice.

154
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:42,740
Later days.

155
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:47,780
After that sunny interaction, the frost between them melted away like the winter snow.

156
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:52,460
You've been in a weirdly good mood since the festival, Yamada.

157
00:06:52,880 --> 00:06:55,800
And I see your eyes darting around, scanning the room for her.

158
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:57,080
But I'm not gonna bite.

159
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:58,800
I am made of stone!

160
00:06:59,180 --> 00:07:00,840
Yamada, are you looking for someone?

161
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,580
Yeah, just Capacho.

162
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:05,580
Oh, now you're just touching me.

163
00:07:05,580 --> 00:07:07,260
But I will not be provoked!

164
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:10,260
I don't know why I'm surprised.

165
00:07:10,980 --> 00:07:12,660
Both Yamada and Tani are good guys.

166
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:16,080
Of course someone likes them.

167
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,940
Of course they can accept that like normal people.

168
00:07:19,620 --> 00:07:21,420
This isn't gonna work, Taira.

169
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:24,160
Your personality's just different than I thought it'd be.

170
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:28,700
I gotta push those memories down.

171
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:34,760
I couldn't be more different from Yamada's dumb friend.

172
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:37,300
Acting like middle school was so great and high school isn't.

173
00:07:37,620 --> 00:07:39,120
What is that guy even talking about?

174
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:43,500
You don't get to choose your elementary or middle school, so they're hell for a lot of people.

175
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:45,740
He could at least acknowledge that much.

176
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:48,080
But even if he did, I think I'd still be chill.

177
00:07:48,080 --> 00:08:00,580
You weren't even saying anything?

178
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:07,020
Need my music time to decompress, okay?

179
00:08:07,020 --> 00:08:08,780
Do you think this is funny too?

180
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:09,760
I'm not laughing.

181
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:11,160
Well, you should jerk.

182
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:16,920
Suspect doesn't typically jerk to the tube, which could only mean he's going into work.

183
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:17,560
Elementary.

184
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:21,100
Shall we take a little detour to the convenience store today, Tani?

185
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:21,920
What? No.

186
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:22,960
Sure, that's fine.

187
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:23,780
It's not though.

188
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:24,840
Well, quick.

189
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:26,700
Just make us some soft serve, please.

190
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:28,760
Our store doesn't have the machine for that.

191
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:32,040
And my shift doesn't start till later, so I won't be able to help you.

192
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:34,740
Aw, we could wait for him, Tani.

193
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:35,940
Or you could go home.

194
00:08:36,540 --> 00:08:37,740
What's that noise for?

195
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,360
And he takes the bait.

196
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:42,020
What does it matter if I'm there or not?

197
00:08:42,040 --> 00:08:43,000
It's just a store.

198
00:08:43,180 --> 00:08:43,400
Huh?

199
00:08:43,780 --> 00:08:45,920
Because it's fun having you around, dummy.

200
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:50,080
Come on, back me up.

201
00:08:50,180 --> 00:08:50,640
It is.

202
00:08:52,820 --> 00:08:53,260
Hmm.

203
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:54,900
Is that so?

204
00:08:54,900 --> 00:09:02,760
Well, I guess it's fun.

205
00:09:04,540 --> 00:09:06,320
I want a free ice cream now.

206
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:06,880
Gimme, gimme.

207
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:08,200
Will you please just leave?

208
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:14,980
It's Yamada.

209
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:17,340
What now?

210
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:18,560
Do I say hello?

211
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:20,500
Starting a conversation?

212
00:09:21,780 --> 00:09:23,080
You should practice on me.

213
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:24,340
I'll be your dummy.

214
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:26,100
I'll do it.

215
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:27,800
Yo, Nishi.

216
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:28,880
Oh.

217
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:32,040
Uh, sorry.

218
00:09:32,180 --> 00:09:33,000
That came out wrong.

219
00:09:33,180 --> 00:09:37,020
I wanted to say hi to you first, but then you said yo, and it sort of caught me off guard.

220
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:39,080
Man, that's good.

221
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:40,540
You're hilarious, Nishi.

222
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,220
He thought I was funny.

223
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:46,400
Um, hey, Hon.

224
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:48,260
Look who's here.

225
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:48,860
Good morning.

226
00:09:51,220 --> 00:09:52,360
Oh, hey, guys.

227
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:54,080
Did you just lose your dentures or what?

228
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:56,840
Seems like you're getting along really well.

229
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:58,160
I guess so.

230
00:09:58,700 --> 00:09:59,820
I need details.

231
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:01,960
What do you think of Yamada so far?

232
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:02,440
Huh?

233
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:07,680
He makes my heart beat fast.

234
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:10,040
But it's like...

235
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:11,300
Like what?

236
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:12,760
I don't know.

237
00:10:12,980 --> 00:10:14,100
It's a strange feeling.

238
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:15,800
I wonder what it could be.

239
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:17,340
It's a strange feeling!

240
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:18,820
I wonder what it could be!

241
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:22,000
What in the heart, I tell, is this?

242
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:24,240
The strange feeling.

243
00:10:24,420 --> 00:10:27,600
Would you say it's like your heart aches for him or burns for him or...

244
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:28,440
Oh, no.

245
00:10:28,940 --> 00:10:30,740
It's nothing fancy like that.

246
00:10:30,940 --> 00:10:31,480
It's not fancy.

247
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:32,240
That helps.

248
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:35,220
I just don't know if it's Yamada or the situation.

249
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:38,860
Like, is my heart beating fast because of him or is it a panic attack?

250
00:10:39,020 --> 00:10:39,720
Oh, okay.

251
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:41,300
We're getting real real today.

252
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:45,780
Every time I talk to a boy, my heart starts pounding like crazy and I don't have enough

253
00:10:45,780 --> 00:10:47,340
experience to understand why.

254
00:10:47,620 --> 00:10:50,980
I can't tell how much of it is Yamada and how much of it is just me.

255
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:52,020
Self-aware.

256
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:52,620
Respect.

257
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:54,420
Well, I'm relieved.

258
00:10:54,740 --> 00:10:58,000
Don't think I could sit through another rom-com where the lead girl's totally dense.

259
00:10:58,200 --> 00:10:58,460
What?

260
00:10:59,020 --> 00:11:00,120
Forget I said anything.

261
00:11:00,900 --> 00:11:04,720
Even if it is just the situation making your heart pound, why does that matter?

262
00:11:04,820 --> 00:11:06,820
Because then it's like anyone would do.

263
00:11:07,020 --> 00:11:08,160
Like I'm using him!

264
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:09,640
Hmm...

265
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:10,960
Is it, though?

266
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:13,340
I say it isn't worth thinking about.

267
00:11:13,860 --> 00:11:15,960
Your heart's beating fast because you're anxious.

268
00:11:16,260 --> 00:11:16,960
No question there.

269
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:21,080
You're just wondering if you'd still feel the same feelings even if it was someone other

270
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:22,920
than Yamada making you feel them, right?

271
00:11:23,340 --> 00:11:24,260
I think so.

272
00:11:24,660 --> 00:11:27,820
But does this hypothetical someone else even exist?

273
00:11:27,820 --> 00:11:28,920
I guess not.

274
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:32,400
So you're pitting Yamada against Schrodinger's cat boy for no reason at all?

275
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:34,480
Those worries aren't real.

276
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:35,140
They're nothing.

277
00:11:35,540 --> 00:11:37,500
You're just pulling new problems out of thin air.

278
00:11:37,740 --> 00:11:38,740
You could do that forever.

279
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:42,120
Get hung up on reality all day, but these pointless what-ifs?

280
00:11:42,340 --> 00:11:43,000
Let him go.

281
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:46,100
Maybe just start with how do I feel about him for now.

282
00:11:46,280 --> 00:11:46,820
You're right.

283
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,580
And honestly, that's enough.

284
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:52,980
But still, I can't even get that far until I can talk without getting nervous.

285
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:54,820
There's no denying that.

286
00:11:54,820 --> 00:12:01,280
Like I said, guys and girls both bleed the same color of red if you stab them.

287
00:12:01,860 --> 00:12:04,220
Reminds me not to get on Hone's bad side.

288
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:06,080
Don't lose any sleep.

289
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:09,960
Just put in some practice and in a while you won't be so nervous anymore.

290
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:12,500
Then you'll know what's making your heart beat so fast.

291
00:12:12,780 --> 00:12:14,300
Or who's making it beat fast.

292
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:17,000
And I'll be right here to back you up the whole time.

293
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:23,580
Hone, you don't get shy around people at all, do you?

294
00:12:23,780 --> 00:12:24,660
I'm so jealous.

295
00:12:25,340 --> 00:12:27,720
I don't think it's a matter of me being shy or not.

296
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:31,680
I have this sort of mild disdain for everyone regardless of their gender.

297
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:33,780
Oh, good for you.

298
00:12:34,040 --> 00:12:34,600
Come on, guys.

299
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:35,080
Let's go.

300
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:35,880
It should have been a foul.

301
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:36,220
No.

302
00:12:38,420 --> 00:12:39,440
Thanks for your help.

303
00:12:39,540 --> 00:12:40,640
It was so busy today.

304
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:41,660
Yeah, of course.

305
00:12:41,660 --> 00:12:48,800
You know, up until recently, Tawny and I hadn't talked much.

306
00:12:49,160 --> 00:12:51,620
My heart would pound because I didn't know what he was thinking.

307
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:53,940
But we talked a little at the festival,

308
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:57,380
so being around him doesn't make me as nervous as it did before.

309
00:13:00,900 --> 00:13:04,380
Way to kill the cops, Suzuki.

310
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:07,380
You sent it flying through the flipping window.

311
00:13:07,760 --> 00:13:08,620
Out of bounds, girl.

312
00:13:08,620 --> 00:13:10,940
I don't control the wind, you big jerks.

313
00:13:11,660 --> 00:13:12,520
It's Tawny!

314
00:13:13,900 --> 00:13:14,920
Oh, Anishi!

315
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:15,520
Yahoo!

316
00:13:16,320 --> 00:13:16,620
What?

317
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:20,060
Hey, since when are you Anishi friends?

318
00:13:20,220 --> 00:13:21,520
I've never seen you guys hang out.

319
00:13:21,740 --> 00:13:22,440
Who cares?

320
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:23,520
We're friends now.

321
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:24,580
Lay down, Anishi.

322
00:13:25,860 --> 00:13:28,000
Oh, I shouldn't have come along.

323
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:29,340
This was a mistake.

324
00:13:30,020 --> 00:13:31,440
I didn't know you played badminton.

325
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:33,080
Oh, the old wacky wacky.

326
00:13:33,380 --> 00:13:34,680
I haven't balled in a while.

327
00:13:34,780 --> 00:13:36,580
Gotta practice or my minton will get bad.

328
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:38,340
There's no ball in badminton.

329
00:13:38,340 --> 00:13:40,140
And your minton is very bad.

330
00:13:40,140 --> 00:13:41,980
Wait, you should be practicing his running.

331
00:13:42,180 --> 00:13:43,760
I've mastered the old wacky job.

332
00:13:43,820 --> 00:13:44,400
You laughed.

333
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:45,540
I'm sorry.

334
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:46,600
It's just...

335
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:48,160
He said I'm minted his back.

336
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:49,560
How is that funny?

337
00:13:52,140 --> 00:13:54,000
I'm so sweaty.

338
00:13:54,120 --> 00:13:55,320
The wind feels extra chilly.

339
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:56,080
Gnarly.

340
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:57,480
Oh, crap.

341
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:58,140
Do I stink?

342
00:13:58,300 --> 00:13:59,060
I went too hard.

343
00:13:59,260 --> 00:13:59,940
Excuse me?

344
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:02,180
Since when do you care about personal hygiene?

345
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:03,700
Did you rehearse that?

346
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:07,580
So, Nishi, you laugh a lot, huh?

347
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:08,000
What?

348
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:11,340
I'm so embarrassed.

349
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:14,260
This is the nervous kind of heart pounding for sure.

350
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:18,760
Yeah, I want to fix that, but I can't tell that sometimes...

351
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:19,400
Fix it?

352
00:14:19,940 --> 00:14:21,280
Why fix something good?

353
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:24,280
I don't think you need to change.

354
00:14:25,120 --> 00:14:25,700
My heart...

355
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:27,060
I'm dying.

356
00:14:27,060 --> 00:14:31,100
Yamada, if you're that worried about stinking, put on some of this.

357
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:31,800
Huh?

358
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:33,160
Oh, thanks.

359
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:35,520
So, uh...

360
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:36,820
What kind is this one?

361
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:38,200
Oh, it's cool, man.

362
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:39,080
Oh!

363
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:40,340
I can't!

364
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:41,820
What is this nap?

365
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:43,420
I'm freezing my napsob!

366
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:43,880
I know.

367
00:14:44,100 --> 00:14:46,000
I hate it, so I figured I'd just give it to you.

368
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:47,760
What, am I a trash can to you?

369
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:52,860
It's easy to make me laugh, but I don't think that's it.

370
00:14:53,160 --> 00:14:56,300
Yamada makes it easy for anyone to laugh when he's around.

371
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:57,600
Told ya!

372
00:15:03,780 --> 00:15:04,340
What?

373
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:05,860
What is happening?

374
00:15:13,460 --> 00:15:14,340
Hey, Tani.

375
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:14,880
Morning.

376
00:15:15,300 --> 00:15:16,040
How are you?

377
00:15:16,420 --> 00:15:17,060
I'm fine.

378
00:15:18,180 --> 00:15:18,620
Yes!

379
00:15:18,860 --> 00:15:20,320
I had a normal human interaction.

380
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:21,760
I'm so sleepy.

381
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:23,480
Whoa!

382
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:32,280
What the...

383
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:34,080
Oh, how's it going, Tani?

384
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:36,480
What did I just witness?

385
00:15:38,060 --> 00:15:41,420
Tani, what were you and Nishi talking about just now?

386
00:15:41,420 --> 00:15:41,600
Huh?

387
00:15:41,980 --> 00:15:42,340
Nishi?

388
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:43,060
Where?

389
00:15:43,060 --> 00:15:43,980
Nothing.

390
00:15:44,220 --> 00:15:45,540
We told each other good morning.

391
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:46,920
Are you sure?

392
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:49,500
She flipped out and ran away over a good morning.

393
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:50,660
I guess.

394
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:51,320
Oh.

395
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:53,080
Hmm.

396
00:15:55,640 --> 00:15:56,640
Quick question.

397
00:15:57,020 --> 00:15:57,160
Hmm?

398
00:15:57,660 --> 00:15:59,580
Can you tell me what Nishi's like?

399
00:15:59,940 --> 00:16:00,200
What?

400
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:04,300
Well, you both work in the library, so you must know her pretty well.

401
00:16:04,660 --> 00:16:05,900
One might say, intimately.

402
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:09,180
Uh, no, I wouldn't say that.

403
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:10,400
Hmm.

404
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:13,140
I see.

405
00:16:16,420 --> 00:16:16,900
Aw.

406
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:19,460
He says the beef katsu rolls are all sold out.

407
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:20,360
That sucks.

408
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:21,960
Hey, Tida.

409
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:23,960
Could I ask for your advice?

410
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:24,260
Huh?

411
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:25,780
Advice from me?

412
00:16:26,740 --> 00:16:27,820
Like, about what?

413
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:33,200
So, Suzuki suddenly developed an interest in the girl who works with you?

414
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:33,980
Yeah.

415
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:38,160
I can tell there's something specific bothering her, but I can't tell what.

416
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:40,600
I mean, it's pretty obvious, right?

417
00:16:41,660 --> 00:16:43,860
She thinks you've got a side piece, duh.

418
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:45,660
A side piece?

419
00:16:45,740 --> 00:16:46,300
Come on.

420
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:48,200
You're spending time with another girl.

421
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:49,540
Of course she's jealous.

422
00:16:49,540 --> 00:16:50,860
You're sure?

423
00:16:51,860 --> 00:16:54,140
I haven't done anything to make her feel that way.

424
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:57,320
To be honest, I can't imagine Suzuki being jealous at all.

425
00:16:57,460 --> 00:16:59,000
She's too positive of a person.

426
00:16:59,320 --> 00:16:59,680
Yay!

427
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:03,000
Fair enough.

428
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:08,480
Well, if Suzuki is jealous, then it's probably because she thinks you're not paying enough attention to her.

429
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:10,260
It's okay to be mad about it.

430
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:11,540
Come on, get mad.

431
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:13,100
Do you want us to fight?

432
00:17:13,760 --> 00:17:14,900
I see what's happening.

433
00:17:15,220 --> 00:17:17,060
You're into the idea that she's jealous.

434
00:17:17,060 --> 00:17:20,280
Of course, it's all coming together now.

435
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:26,800
A part of you wants her to be jealous because it validates your worth as a boyfriend, even if it's not exactly in character for her.

436
00:17:27,100 --> 00:17:30,180
But you're still not confident, so you need validation from me, too.

437
00:17:30,520 --> 00:17:31,260
Is that it?

438
00:17:31,260 --> 00:17:33,420
Sorry, it's not like that at all.

439
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:35,400
Or is it?

440
00:17:36,020 --> 00:17:36,440
Wait.

441
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:38,180
Huh?

442
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,780
It's you guys.

443
00:17:40,080 --> 00:17:41,440
When did you start hanging out?

444
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:45,880
Geez, overreact much?

445
00:17:46,220 --> 00:17:47,340
Sorry, I guess.

446
00:17:47,340 --> 00:17:50,680
What's up today?

447
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:52,200
Working in the library again?

448
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:53,060
Yep.

449
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:55,460
Meaning Neishi will be there, too.

450
00:17:56,100 --> 00:17:57,080
Mm-hmm.

451
00:17:57,220 --> 00:17:57,600
Yeah.

452
00:17:58,940 --> 00:17:59,260
I see.

453
00:17:59,700 --> 00:18:00,280
Roger that.

454
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:02,640
Suzuki, is something bothering you?

455
00:18:02,940 --> 00:18:04,180
Check it out!

456
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:06,620
Toy central, baby!

457
00:18:07,180 --> 00:18:08,700
I love this stuff!

458
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:10,180
Yamada, remember D?

459
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:11,520
Whoa!

460
00:18:11,980 --> 00:18:12,760
Oh, hell yeah!

461
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:15,980
I missed my chance to ask her.

462
00:18:20,280 --> 00:18:22,200
I was able to say hi to Tani.

463
00:18:22,420 --> 00:18:25,400
The second I saw Yamada, I folded out of there like a weirdo.

464
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:29,420
I thought I was finally getting better at talking to him, but now I'm getting worse.

465
00:18:29,620 --> 00:18:30,660
I'm devolving!

466
00:18:33,740 --> 00:18:35,040
I see what's happening.

467
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:37,080
You're into the idea that she's jealous.

468
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:38,520
Is that true?

469
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:43,620
No.

470
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:48,060
If I'm happy because she's worrying, then that means our relationship isn't equal.

471
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:49,540
Also...

472
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:53,780
Even if your mind is cloudy or you're still processing something, I want you to know that

473
00:18:53,780 --> 00:18:57,240
if you ever feel anxious or on edge about anything, you can talk to me.

474
00:18:58,020 --> 00:19:00,140
I want to be that way for her, too.

475
00:19:03,860 --> 00:19:06,940
If there's something she wants to say, I want to hear it.

476
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:09,040
She shouldn't feel anxious about us.

477
00:19:09,220 --> 00:19:10,560
I don't want to be the cause of that.

478
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:13,780
If she suspects me of something, that's my own fault.

479
00:19:14,580 --> 00:19:17,020
This is turning into a replay of Summer Break.

480
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:19,980
At this rate, I'm going to end up with the exact same regrets.

481
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:23,400
Even if I'm scared, I can't run away next time.

482
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:26,880
There's no point in wondering what she's thinking or how she's feeling.

483
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:29,200
I won't find the answer on my own.

484
00:19:29,360 --> 00:19:31,440
I'm just making up fears for myself.

485
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:32,700
It's getting pathetic.

486
00:19:33,080 --> 00:19:34,340
The next time I see her...

487
00:19:34,340 --> 00:19:35,740
The next time I see him...

488
00:19:35,740 --> 00:19:36,640
I'll just ask.

489
00:19:36,700 --> 00:19:37,840
I'll just talk to him.

490
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:52,360
What up, Nishi?

491
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:54,040
Oh, and Tani, too.

492
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:54,940
Team Lebe!

493
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:57,760
Oh, come on.

494
00:19:57,900 --> 00:19:58,580
Say something.

495
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:01,260
I'm losing it already.

496
00:20:01,780 --> 00:20:04,060
Now that the moment's here, I can't look him in the eye.

497
00:20:04,060 --> 00:20:14,880
Suzu King?

498
00:20:15,740 --> 00:20:16,640
Yo, Nishi!

499
00:20:17,660 --> 00:20:18,900
Come and blow bubbles!

500
00:20:20,660 --> 00:20:24,660
You missed out on the other stuff, but you're here just in time for Bubba-palooza.

501
00:20:25,440 --> 00:20:26,640
Uh, Bubba-palooza?

502
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:28,840
You're a star, so you can take this one.

503
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:31,480
Yamada's got the bubble juice right over there.

504
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:32,480
Um...

505
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:38,800
I'm so happy!

506
00:20:39,700 --> 00:20:40,460
Thank you!

507
00:20:40,560 --> 00:20:41,920
I'll never forget this kindness!

508
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:44,720
Okay, Fancy!

509
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:45,600
Hi, buddy!

510
00:20:45,600 --> 00:20:56,060
I've got you now.

511
00:20:57,640 --> 00:21:00,060
So, Nishi, you laugh a lot, huh?

512
00:21:00,320 --> 00:21:00,580
What?

513
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:02,340
Now that I think about it...

514
00:21:02,340 --> 00:21:04,700
I got my glove out to catch feelings, you know?

515
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:07,660
Same school?

516
00:21:07,920 --> 00:21:08,720
Different class?

517
00:21:09,020 --> 00:21:09,460
Shy?

518
00:21:09,460 --> 00:21:12,220
Fix it.

519
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:13,500
Why fix something good?

520
00:21:15,420 --> 00:21:17,000
I don't think you need to change.

521
00:21:17,360 --> 00:21:17,860
Look!

522
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:18,440
It's her!

523
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:19,400
It's totally her!

524
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:20,740
Yamada's got Nishi fever!

525
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:22,460
Then this morning...

526
00:21:24,220 --> 00:21:24,740
No!

527
00:21:26,620 --> 00:21:27,760
What the...

528
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:29,560
Oh, how's it going, Tani?

529
00:21:30,060 --> 00:21:31,480
What did I just witness?

530
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:35,760
Her face with tomato machine bolted after seeing Yamada!

531
00:21:35,760 --> 00:21:36,360
Whoa!

532
00:21:36,540 --> 00:21:37,520
This is moving fast!

533
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:40,200
They've already made a left connection!

534
00:21:42,360 --> 00:21:45,560
Good thing I kept Yamada here till the library closed!

535
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:47,760
Suzuki...

536
00:21:47,760 --> 00:21:51,020
Why did you ask me about Nishi so many times today?

537
00:21:51,660 --> 00:21:51,880
Huh?

538
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:53,180
Oh, yeah.

539
00:21:53,580 --> 00:21:56,160
I wanted to learn more about her so she could be my new buddy.

540
00:21:56,420 --> 00:21:57,600
And you do work with her!

541
00:21:57,760 --> 00:22:00,240
Can you tell me what Nishi's like?

542
00:22:00,240 --> 00:22:04,040
Zero subtext.

